msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "American pickerel"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"An American pickerel.  It looks like a pike, but unlike its chain pickerel "
"cousin, this one is way smaller."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "muskellunge"
msgid_plural "muskellunges"
msgstr[0] "щука-маскинонг"
msgstr[1] "щуки-маскинонга"
msgstr[2] "щук-маскинонгов"
msgstr[3] "щуки-маскинонги"

#. ~ Description of monster "muskellunge"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A muskellunge.  Closely related to pike but even larger, it shares the same "
"aggression and sharp teeth."
msgstr ""
"Щука-максинонг, близкий и более крупный родственник обыкновенной щуки, точно"
" такая же агрессивная острозубая рыба."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "white sucker"
msgid_plural "white suckers"
msgstr[0] "белый чукучан"
msgstr[1] "белых чукучана"
msgstr[2] "белых чукучанов"
msgstr[3] "белые чукучаны"

#. ~ Description of monster "white sucker"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A white sucker.  It has a streamlined body with a round mouth."
msgstr "Белый чукучан, рыба с округлым телом и круглым ртом."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "European carp"
msgid_plural "European carp"
msgstr[0] "европейский карп"
msgstr[1] "европейских карпа"
msgstr[2] "европейских карпов"
msgstr[3] "европейские карпы"

#. ~ Description of monster "European carp"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A golden-yellow common carp.  Some people think they don't taste great, but "
"you can't afford to be choosy in the Cataclysm."
msgstr ""
"Золотисто-жёлтый обыкновенный карп. Некоторые думают, что он не очень "
"вкусный, но Катаклизм — не время, когда можно позволить себе привередничать."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "grass carp"
msgid_plural "grass carps"
msgstr[0] "белый амур"
msgstr[1] "белых амура"
msgstr[2] "белых амуров"
msgstr[3] "белые амуры"

#. ~ Description of monster "grass carp"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A huge grass carp.  A golden, herbivorous fish."
msgstr "Огромный белый амур. Слегка золотистая травоядная рыба."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "goldfish"
msgid_plural "goldfish"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "goldfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"Yes, this is that common pet fish.  Though, given its size and the fact that"
" it's still alive, you can take a wild guess that this one is feral."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "bowfin"
msgid_plural "bowfins"
msgstr[0] "амия"
msgstr[1] "амии"
msgstr[2] "амий"
msgstr[3] "амии"

#. ~ Description of monster "bowfin"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A bowfin.  These fish are related to gar but without the huge teeth, skin-"
"rending scales, and aggression."
msgstr ""
"Ильная рыба. Состоит в родстве в панцирной щукой, но без её огромных зубов, "
"раздирающей кожу чешуи и агрессии."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "longnose gar"
msgid_plural "longnose gars"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "longnose gar"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A large ancient type of fish with a mean jaw and poisonous eggs."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "burbot"
msgid_plural "burbots"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "burbot"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A relatively large fish that looks like a cross between a catfish and an "
"eel, and is the only freshwater fish from the order that cods hail from."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "lake sturgeon"
msgid_plural "lake sturgeons"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "lake sturgeon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A very large armored bottom-feeder, the lake sturgeon is one of the largest "
"unmutated fish one can find in the freshwater regions of New England."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "shortnose sturgeon"
msgid_plural "shortnose sturgeons"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "shortnose sturgeon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"While the shortnose sturgeon is still large, it is nothing compared to its "
"cousin - the lake sturgeon.  What really sets it apart, however, is its "
"signature shorter snout."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "fallfish"
msgid_plural "fallfish"
msgstr[0] "сильный семотилус"
msgstr[1] "сильных семотилуса"
msgstr[2] "сильных семотилусов"
msgstr[3] "сильные семотилусы"

#. ~ Description of monster "fallfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "A fallfish.  These fish are small cyprinids, related to carp."
msgstr ""
"Сильный семотилус. Это североамериканская пресноводная рыба, голавль из "
"семейства карповых"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "lobster"
msgid_plural "lobsters"
msgstr[0] "омар"
msgstr[1] "омара"
msgstr[2] "омаров"
msgstr[3] "омары"

#. ~ Description of monster "lobster"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A dark greenish crustacean in its natural habitat.  These were once "
"considered pests barely worth eating, then some marketing genius started "
"selling them to people as a delicacy and they took off in popularity… and "
"price."
msgstr ""
"Тёмно-зелёное ракообразное в естественной среде обитания. Когда-то этих "
"животных считали вредителями, которых и есть-то не стоит. Но затем один "
"гений маркетинга начал продавать их как деликатес, и их популярность "
"взлетела… Как и цена."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "crayfish"
msgid_plural "crayfish"
msgstr[0] "рак"
msgstr[1] "рака"
msgstr[2] "раков"
msgstr[3] "раки"

#. ~ Description of monster "crayfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"This crustacean looks like a tiny lobster, but is actually a completely "
"different species.  If you could get ahold of a bunch more of these, a hefty"
" pot of boiling water, and some spicy seasonings…"
msgstr ""
"Хоть это ракообразное и похоже на маленького лобстера, на самом деле это "
"совершенно разные виды. Эх, вот бы найти немного больше этих штук, "
"здоровенную кастрюлю с кипящей водой и чутка пряных приправ..."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "crustacean larva"
msgid_plural "crustacean larvae"
msgstr[0] "личинка ракообразных"
msgstr[1] "личинки ракообразных"
msgstr[2] "личинок ракообразных"
msgstr[3] "личинки ракообразных"

#. ~ Description of monster "crustacean larva"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A minuscule half-translucent crustacean larva.  Impossible to identify which"
" species it belongs to."
msgstr ""
"Крошечная полупрозрачная личинка рачка. Невозможно определить, к какому виду"
" он принадлежит."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "American eel"
msgid_plural "American eels"
msgstr[0] "американский угорь"
msgstr[1] "американских угря"
msgstr[2] "американских угрей"
msgstr[3] "американские угри"

#. ~ Description of monster "American eel"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"An American eel.  They used to be quite common in these parts until the dams"
" were built.  They'll get a second chance now that those aren't running."
msgstr ""
"Американский угорь. Они были довольно распространены в этих местах, пока "
"здесь не были построены дамбы. Теперь дамбы не работают, так что у них "
"появился второй шанс"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "oversized crayfish"
msgid_plural "oversized crayfish"
msgstr[0] "большой рак"
msgstr[1] "больших рака"
msgstr[2] "больших раков"
msgstr[3] "большие раки"

#. ~ Description of monster "oversized crayfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A mutant crayfish the size of a dog, with a brown carapace, claws, and long "
"antennae."
msgstr ""
"Рак-мутант размером с собаку с коричневым панцирем, клешнями и длинными "
"усиками."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/fish.json
msgid "giant crayfish"
msgid_plural "giant crayfish"
msgstr[0] "гигантский рак"
msgstr[1] "гигантских рака"
msgstr[2] "гигантских раков"
msgstr[3] "гигантские раки"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant crayfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A mutant, terrestrial variety of crayfish, this massive crustacean resembles"
" a humongous lobster."
msgstr ""
"Мутировавшая разновидность сигнальных раков, массивное ракообразное "
"существо."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/fish.json
msgid "colossal crayfish"
msgid_plural "colossal crayfish"
msgstr[0] "рак-колосс"
msgstr[1] "рака-колосса"
msgstr[2] "раков-колоссов"
msgstr[3] "раки-колоссы"

#. ~ Description of monster "colossal crayfish"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "An enormous mutated gray crayfish with pincer claws and long antennae."
msgstr "Огромный серый рак-мутант с клешнями и длинными усиками."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/fish.json
msgid "giant crayfish larva"
msgid_plural "giant crayfish larvae"
msgstr[0] "личинка гигантского рака"
msgstr[1] "личинки гигантского рака"
msgstr[2] "личинок гигантского рака"
msgstr[3] "личинки гигантского рака"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant crayfish larva"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A large crayfish larva already larger than non-mutated adults of its kind."
msgstr ""
"Личинка гиганского рака уже крупнее немутировавших взрослых особей своего "
"вида."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "razorclaw"
msgid_plural "razorclaws"
msgstr[0] "бритвокоготь"
msgstr[1] "бритвокогтя"
msgstr[2] "бритвокогтей"
msgstr[3] "бритвокогти"

#. ~ Description of monster "razorclaw"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A man-sized crustacean clad in iron-like chitin, capable of emitting "
"horrible shrieking noises.  Often spotted near shipwrecks or other dark, "
"damp places, which it uses as nesting grounds."
msgstr ""
"Ракообразное размером с человека в твёрдом как железо хитиновом панцире, "
"способное издавать самый ужасающий вопль. Их часто видят поблизости "
"кораблекрушений или других темных влажных мест, в которых они устраивают "
"гнёзда."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "giant carp"
msgid_plural "giant carps"
msgstr[0] "гигантский карп"
msgstr[1] "гигантских карпа"
msgstr[2] "гигантских карпов"
msgstr[3] "гигантские карпы"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant carp"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"This thing looks like a carp, but huge and very, very angry.  Death is the "
"gift of the carp god."
msgstr ""
"Эта штука похожа на карпа, только огромного и очень-очень сердитого. Смерть "
"— подарок бога карпов."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "giant salmon"
msgid_plural "giant salmons"
msgstr[0] "гигантский лосось"
msgstr[1] "гигантских лосося"
msgstr[2] "гигантских лососей"
msgstr[3] "гигантские лососи"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant salmon"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A mutated salmon, the size of a large dog and quite dangerous to the "
"inexperienced angler."
msgstr ""
"Мутировавший лосось. Размером с большую собаку, он весьма опасен для "
"неопытного рыболова."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid "seweranha"
msgid_plural "seweranhas"
msgstr[0] "канализапиранья"
msgstr[1] "канализапираньи"
msgstr[2] "канализапираний"
msgstr[3] "канализапираньи"

#. ~ Description of monster "seweranha"
#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
msgid ""
"A large, mutant variety of carp.  It has shimmering green scales and a mouth"
" lined with three jagged rows of razor-sharp teeth."
msgstr ""
"Разновидность большого мутировавшего карпа. У него блестящая чешуя и пасть с"
" тремя рядами острых как бритва зубов."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid "fungal blossom"
msgid_plural "fungal blossoms"
msgstr[0] "грибной цветок"
msgstr[1] "грибных цветка"
msgstr[2] "грибных цветков"
msgstr[3] "грибные цветки"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal blossom"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid ""
"A broad fungus, looking much like a glowing blue sunflower.  It appears to "
"emit finer spores than the typical fungal emission."
msgstr ""
"Широкий гриб, очень похожий на светящийся синий подсолнух. Кажется, что он "
"испускает более мелкие, чем при обычном грибном выбросе, споры."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid "fungal hedgerow"
msgid_plural "fungal hedgerows"
msgstr[0] "грибная изгородь"
msgstr[1] "грибной изгороди"
msgstr[2] "грибной изгороди"
msgstr[3] "грибная изгородь"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal hedgerow"
#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
msgid ""
"Looking at first glance like a dull gray privet, this \"hedge\" is really a "
"mass of barbed fungal tendrils, defending the fungal tower."
msgstr ""
"Выглядящая на первый взгляд как тускло-серая бирючина, эта «изгородь» на "
"самом деле скопление колючих грибных усиков, защищающих грибную башню."

